# `.btc` → CRP Mapping

A `.btc` identifier resolves only to an address. A CRP path resolves
to a deterministic semantic root: dependencies, schema, and execution
steps reconstructible from state alone.

The mapping below is canonical for the AI Agent bundle.

| `.btc` name              | CRP path                       | Role                |
|--------------------------|--------------------------------|---------------------|
| `aiagentframework.btc`   | `root.aiagent`                 | System root         |
| `aiagentidentity.btc`    | `root.aiagent.identity`        | Agent identity      |
| `aiagentcredential.btc`  | `root.aiagent.credential`      | Credential layer    |
| `aiagentlicense.btc`     | `root.aiagent.license`         | License layer       |
| `aiagentengine.btc`      | `root.aiagent.engine`          | Execution engine    |
| `aiagentlayer.btc`       | `root.aiagent.layer`           | Integration layer   |
| `aiagentfinance.btc`     | `root.aiagent.finance`         | Financial logic     |
| `aiagentledger.btc`      | `root.aiagent.ledger`          | State ledger        |
| `aiagentgovernance.btc`  | `root.aiagent.governance`      | Governance layer    |

This demo implements three of these paths to keep the resolver
minimal and the property observable. Adding the others is an
exercise in writing more transitions — not in changing the protocol.
